# Morrow leaves the interfaces to NetworkManager (nmtui, or `nmcli`).
#
# Alpine's base install brings up an `automatic` interface from this file with busybox udhcpc, and
# NetworkManager manages the same interfaces by default. Two managers on one interface is not a
# conflict that announces itself: it is a machine whose connection drops every few minutes for no
# visible reason. NetworkManager configures ethernet and wifi on its own, so the only job left here
# is loopback -- and the installer leaves an existing configuration alone rather than discarding
# somebody's static address on their behalf.
auto lo
iface lo inet loopback
